-- Delaware General Corporation Law, 8 Del. C. ch. 1, Subchapter XIII (ss 321-330): SUITS AGAINST CORPORATIONS,
-- DIRECTORS, OFFICERS OR STOCKHOLDERS. Layer 1: the law, objectively, from the text alone (src:1632-1679).
--
-- The source is the plain-text rendering de-code-t8-ch1-2026-10-01.txt of the Delaware Code Online; it is not the
-- official text. Quote lines below are slices of that file: `-- src:N | ...` is line N, and an ellipsis means the
-- line goes on.
--
-- Conventions: every rule is named with its section locator first (`s 324(b) ...`); a fact another section or another
-- statute decides is an input, marked `-- out of range: section N (piece X)`; a case the text does not answer is
-- NOTHING in a MAYBE; time limits use the core's Period and `the date ... after`; the last day of a period of days
-- is inside the period (fork F1 in NOTES.md).
--
-- SEAT (Layer 2 is in dg10-seat.l4): a person who incorporates, directs or holds stock in a Delaware corporation.
-- In this subchapter that person is a defendant officer, director or stockholder, a plaintiff creditor or
-- stockholder, a stockholder whose shares are attached, or the person served for the corporation.

§ `Subchapter XIII. Suits Against Corporations, Directors, Officers or Stockholders`

§§ `s 321 Service of process on corporations`

-- src:1635 | Service of legal process upon any corporation of this State shall be made by delivering a copy personally to any officer or director of the corporation in this State, or the registered agent of the corporation in this State, or by leaving it at the dwelling house or usual place of abode in this State of any officer, director or registered agent (if the registered agent be an individual), or at the registered office or other place of business of the corporation in this State. …
-- src:1635 | If the registered agent be a corporation, service of process upon it as such agent may be made by serving, in this State, a copy thereof on the president, vice-president, secretary, assistant secretary or any director of the corporate registered agent. …
@ref 8 Del. C. § 321(a) (src:1635)
DECLARE `s 321(a) Way of serving process on the corporation` IS ONE OF
    `a copy delivered personally in this State to an officer or director under s 321(a)`
    `a copy delivered personally in this State to the registered agent under s 321(a)`
    `a copy left at the dwelling house or usual place of abode in this State of an officer, director or individual registered agent under s 321(a)`
    `a copy left at the registered office of the corporation in this State under s 321(a)`
    `a copy left at another place of business of the corporation in this State under s 321(a)`
    `a copy served in this State on the president, vice-president, secretary, assistant secretary or a director of the corporate registered agent under s 321(a)`
    `a way of service that s 321(a) does not list`

-- The date and the three yes/no facts are read only for a copy left at an abode, the registered office or another
-- place of business; the last yes/no fact only for process returnable forthwith.
-- src:1635 | Service by copy left at the dwelling house or usual place of abode of any officer, director or registered agent, or at the registered office or other place of business of the corporation in this State, to be effective must be delivered thereat at least 6 days before the return date of the process, and in the presence of an adult person, and the officer serving the process shall distinctly state the manner of service in such person’s return thereto. Process returnable forthwith must be delivered personally to the officer, director or registered agent.
@ref 8 Del. C. § 321(a) (src:1635)
DECLARE `s 321(a) Service of process` HAS
    `the way the process was served`                                                        IS A `s 321(a) Way of serving process on the corporation`
    `the date the copy was left`                                                            IS A DATE
    `the return date of the process`                                                        IS A DATE
    `the copy was left in the presence of an adult person`                                  IS A BOOLEAN
    `the officer serving the process distinctly stated the manner of service in the return` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the process is returnable forthwith`                                                   IS A BOOLEAN

-- "delivered personally to the officer, director or registered agent": a copy delivered personally to an officer or
-- director, to the registered agent, or (for a corporate registered agent) served on its president and the others
-- named (fork F2 in NOTES.md).
-- src:1635 | Process returnable forthwith must be delivered personally to the officer, director or registered agent.
@ref 8 Del. C. § 321(a) (src:1635)
GIVEN service IS A `s 321(a) Service of process`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 321(a) the process was delivered personally to the officer, director or registered agent` service MEANS
    CONSIDER service's `the way the process was served`
    WHEN `a copy delivered personally in this State to an officer or director under s 321(a)` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `a copy delivered personally in this State to the registered agent under s 321(a)` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `a copy served in this State on the president, vice-president, secretary, assistant secretary or a director of the corporate registered agent under s 321(a)` THEN TRUE
    OTHERWISE FALSE

-- "to be effective must be delivered thereat at least 6 days before the return date, in presence of an adult person,
-- and the officer serving the process shall distinctly state the manner of service in such person's return"
-- The copy must be left on or before the sixth day before the return date (fork F1).
-- src:1635 | Service by copy left at the dwelling house or usual place of abode of any officer, director or registered agent, or at the registered office or other place of business of the corporation in this State, to be effective must be delivered thereat at least 6 days before the return date of the process, and in the presence of an adult person, and the officer serving the process shall distinctly state the manner of service in such person’s return thereto. …
@ref 8 Del. C. § 321(a) (src:1635)
GIVEN service IS A `s 321(a) Service of process`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 321(a) a copy left at an abode or place of business was delivered as the subsection requires` service MEANS
        service's `the date the copy was left` AT MOST (`the date` (`period in days` 6) `before` (service's `the return date of the process`))
    AND service's `the copy was left in the presence of an adult person`
    AND service's `the officer serving the process distinctly stated the manner of service in the return`

-- Service under subsection (a) alone; subsections (b) and (c) give two more routes (see the section-wide rule below).
-- src:1635 | Service of legal process upon any corporation of this State shall be made by delivering a copy personally to any officer or director of the corporation in this State, or the registered agent of the corporation in this State, or by leaving it at the dwelling house or usual place of abode in this State of any officer, director or registered agent (if the registered agent be an individual), or at the registered office or other place of business of the corporation in this State. If the registered agent be a corporation, service of process upon it as such agent may be made by serving, in this State, a copy thereof on the president, vice-president, secretary, assistant secretary or any director of the corporate registered agent. Service by copy left at the dwelling house or usual place of abode of any officer, director or registered agent, or at the registered office or other place of business of the corporation in this State, to be effective must be delivered thereat at least 6 days before the return date of the process, and in the presence of an adult person, and the officer serving the process shall distinctly state the manner of service in such person’s return thereto. Process returnable forthwith must be delivered personally to the officer, director or registered agent.
@ref 8 Del. C. § 321(a) (src:1635)
GIVEN service IS A `s 321(a) Service of process`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 321(a) service is effective under subsection (a)` service MEANS
        (CONSIDER service's `the way the process was served`
         WHEN `a copy delivered personally in this State to an officer or director under s 321(a)` THEN TRUE
         WHEN `a copy delivered personally in this State to the registered agent under s 321(a)` THEN TRUE
         WHEN `a copy served in this State on the president, vice-president, secretary, assistant secretary or a director of the corporate registered agent under s 321(a)` THEN TRUE
         WHEN `a copy left at the dwelling house or usual place of abode in this State of an officer, director or individual registered agent under s 321(a)` THEN `s 321(a) a copy left at an abode or place of business was delivered as the subsection requires` service
         WHEN `a copy left at the registered office of the corporation in this State under s 321(a)` THEN `s 321(a) a copy left at an abode or place of business was delivered as the subsection requires` service
         WHEN `a copy left at another place of business of the corporation in this State under s 321(a)` THEN `s 321(a) a copy left at an abode or place of business was delivered as the subsection requires` service
         OTHERWISE FALSE)
    AND (    (NOT service's `the process is returnable forthwith`)
          OR `s 321(a) the process was delivered personally to the officer, director or registered agent` service)

-- (b): "In case the officer whose duty it is to serve legal process cannot by due diligence serve the process in any
-- manner provided for by subsection (a) ... it shall be lawful to serve the process against the corporation upon the
-- Secretary of State ... Process may be served upon the Secretary of State under this subsection by means of
-- electronic transmission but only as prescribed by the Secretary of State."
-- src:1636 | In case the officer whose duty it is to serve legal process cannot by due diligence serve the process in any manner provided for by subsection (a) of this section, it shall be lawful to serve the process against the corporation upon the Secretary of State, and such service shall be as effectual for all intents and purposes as if made in any of the ways provided for in subsection (a) of this section. Process may be served upon the Secretary of State under this subsection by means of electronic transmission but only as prescribed by the Secretary of State. …
@ref 8 Del. C. § 321(b) (src:1636)
GIVEN `the process server could not by due diligence serve the process in any manner provided in s 321(a)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the process was served on the Secretary of State by electronic transmission` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the Secretary of State has prescribed service by electronic transmission in the way it was made` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 321(b) service on the Secretary of State is as effectual as service under subsection (a)` `the process server could not by due diligence serve the process in any manner provided in s 321(a)` `the process was served on the Secretary of State by electronic transmission` `the Secretary of State has prescribed service by electronic transmission in the way it was made` MEANS
        `the process server could not by due diligence serve the process in any manner provided in s 321(a)`
    AND (    (NOT `the process was served on the Secretary of State by electronic transmission`)
          OR `the Secretary of State has prescribed service by electronic transmission in the way it was made`)

-- "directed to the corporation at its principal place of business as it appears on the records relating to such
-- corporation on file with the Secretary of State or, if no such address appears, at its last registered office"
-- src:1636 | the Secretary of State shall forthwith notify the corporation by letter, directed to the corporation at its principal place of business as it appears on the records relating to such corporation on file with the Secretary of State or, if no such address appears, at its last registered office. …
@ref 8 Del. C. § 321(b) (src:1636)
GIVEN `an address for the principal place of business appears on the records on file with the Secretary of State` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the letter was directed to that principal place of business` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the letter was directed to the last registered office of the corporation` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 321(b) the letter is addressed as the subsection requires` `an address for the principal place of business appears on the records on file with the Secretary of State` `the letter was directed to that principal place of business` `the letter was directed to the last registered office of the corporation` MEANS
    IF `an address for the principal place of business appears on the records on file with the Secretary of State`
    THEN `the letter was directed to that principal place of business`
    ELSE `the letter was directed to the last registered office of the corporation`

-- src:1637 | Service upon corporations may also be made in accordance with § 3111 of Title 10 or any other statute or rule of court.
@ref 8 Del. C. § 321(c) (src:1637)
GIVEN `the service was made in accordance with s 3111 of Title 10 or another statute or rule of court` IS A BOOLEAN  -- Title 10 is not among the inputs
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 321(c) service is made in accordance with s 3111 of Title 10 or another statute or rule of court` `the service was made in accordance with s 3111 of Title 10 or another statute or rule of court` MEANS
    `the service was made in accordance with s 3111 of Title 10 or another statute or rule of court`

-- The three routes together: subsection (a), subsection (b), or subsection (c).
-- src:1635 | Service of legal process upon any corporation of this State shall be made by delivering a copy personally to any officer or director of the corporation in this State, or the registered agent of the corporation in this State, or by leaving it at the dwelling house or usual place of abode in this State of any officer, director or registered agent (if the registered agent be an individual), or at the registered office or other place of business of the corporation in this State. …
-- src:1636 | it shall be lawful to serve the process against the corporation upon the Secretary of State, and such service shall be as effectual for all intents and purposes as if made in any of the ways provided for in subsection (a) of this section. …
-- src:1637 | Service upon corporations may also be made in accordance with § 3111 of Title 10 or any other statute or rule of court.
@ref 8 Del. C. § 321 (src:1635-1637)
GIVEN service IS A `s 321(a) Service of process`
      `the process server could not by due diligence serve the process in any manner provided in s 321(a)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the process was served on the Secretary of State by electronic transmission` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the Secretary of State has prescribed service by electronic transmission in the way it was made` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the service was made in accordance with s 3111 of Title 10 or another statute or rule of court` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 321 service of process on the corporation is effective` service `the process server could not by due diligence serve the process in any manner provided in s 321(a)` `the process was served on the Secretary of State by electronic transmission` `the Secretary of State has prescribed service by electronic transmission in the way it was made` `the service was made in accordance with s 3111 of Title 10 or another statute or rule of court` MEANS
        `s 321(a) service is effective under subsection (a)` service
    OR  `s 321(b) service on the Secretary of State is as effectual as service under subsection (a)` `the process server could not by due diligence serve the process in any manner provided in s 321(a)` `the process was served on the Secretary of State by electronic transmission` `the Secretary of State has prescribed service by electronic transmission in the way it was made`
    OR  `s 321(c) service is made in accordance with s 3111 of Title 10 or another statute or rule of court` `the service was made in accordance with s 3111 of Title 10 or another statute or rule of court`

§§ `s 322 Failure of corporation to obey order of court; appointment of receiver`

-- src:1641 | Whenever any corporation shall refuse, fail or neglect to obey any order or decree of any court of this State within the time fixed by the court for its observance, such refusal, failure or neglect shall be a sufficient ground for the appointment of a receiver of the corporation by the Court of Chancery. If the corporation be a foreign corporation, such refusal, failure or neglect shall be a sufficient ground for the appointment of a receiver of the assets of the corporation within this State.
@ref 8 Del. C. § 322 (src:1641)
DECLARE `s 322 Receiver that the Court of Chancery may appoint` IS ONE OF
    `no receiver on the ground in s 322`
    `a receiver of the corporation under s 322`
    `a receiver of the assets of the corporation within this State under s 322`

-- "sufficient ground for the appointment": the Court of Chancery has the ground; the text does not say it must
-- appoint (fork F3). A foreign corporation is one organized under the laws of a jurisdiction other than this State
-- (s 371(a), encoded in dg10-foreign.l4).
-- src:1641 | Whenever any corporation shall refuse, fail or neglect to obey any order or decree of any court of this State within the time fixed by the court for its observance, such refusal, failure or neglect shall be a sufficient ground for the appointment of a receiver of the corporation by the Court of Chancery. If the corporation be a foreign corporation, such refusal, failure or neglect shall be a sufficient ground for the appointment of a receiver of the assets of the corporation within this State.
@ref 8 Del. C. § 322 (src:1641)
GIVEN `the corporation refused, failed or neglected to obey an order or decree of a court of this State within the time fixed by the court` IS A BOOLEAN
      `where the corporation was organized` IS A `Where an entity is formed`
GIVETH A `s 322 Receiver that the Court of Chancery may appoint`
`s 322 the receiver for which the failure to obey is a sufficient ground` `the corporation refused, failed or neglected to obey an order or decree of a court of this State within the time fixed by the court` `where the corporation was organized` MEANS
    IF `the corporation refused, failed or neglected to obey an order or decree of a court of this State within the time fixed by the court`
    THEN (IF `where the corporation was organized` EQUALS `this State`
          THEN `a receiver of the corporation under s 322`
          ELSE `a receiver of the assets of the corporation within this State under s 322`)
    ELSE `no receiver on the ground in s 322`

§§ `s 323 Failure of corporation to obey writ of mandamus; quo warranto proceedings for forfeiture of charter`

-- src:1645 | If any corporation fails to obey the mandate of any peremptory writ of mandamus issued by a court of competent jurisdiction of this State for a period of 30 days after the serving of the writ upon the corporation in any manner as provided by the laws of this State for the service of writs, any party in interest in the proceeding in which the writ of mandamus issued may file a statement of such fact prepared by such party or such party’s attorney with the Attorney General of this State, and it shall thereupon be the duty of the Attorney General to forthwith commence proceedings of quo warranto against the corporation in a court of competent jurisdiction, and the court, upon competent proof of such state of facts and proper proceedings had in such proceeding in quo warranto, shall decree the charter of the corporation forfeited.
@ref 8 Del. C. § 323 (src:1645)
DECLARE `s 323 Failure to obey a peremptory writ of mandamus` HAS
    `the number of days the corporation has failed to obey the writ since it was served on the corporation` IS A NUMBER
    `the person is a party in interest in the proceeding in which the writ issued`                          IS A BOOLEAN
    `the statement of the failure was prepared by that party or that party's attorney`                      IS A BOOLEAN
    `the statement has been filed with the Attorney General`                                                IS A BOOLEAN
    `the court has competent proof of the failure and proper proceedings have been had in quo warranto`     IS A BOOLEAN

-- "for a period of 30 days after the serving of the writ": 30 days must have passed (fork F4).
-- src:1645 | any party in interest in the proceeding in which the writ of mandamus issued may file a statement of such fact prepared by such party or such party’s attorney with the Attorney General of this State, …
@ref 8 Del. C. § 323 (src:1645)
GIVEN failure IS A `s 323 Failure to obey a peremptory writ of mandamus`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 323 the party in interest may file a statement with the Attorney General` failure MEANS
        failure's `the number of days the corporation has failed to obey the writ since it was served on the corporation` AT LEAST 30
    AND failure's `the person is a party in interest in the proceeding in which the writ issued`
    AND failure's `the statement of the failure was prepared by that party or that party's attorney`

-- src:1645 | it shall thereupon be the duty of the Attorney General to forthwith commence proceedings of quo warranto against the corporation …
@ref 8 Del. C. § 323 (src:1645)
GIVEN failure IS A `s 323 Failure to obey a peremptory writ of mandamus`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 323 the Attorney General must forthwith commence quo warranto proceedings against the corporation` failure MEANS
        `s 323 the party in interest may file a statement with the Attorney General` failure
    AND failure's `the statement has been filed with the Attorney General`

-- src:1645 | and the court, upon competent proof of such state of facts and proper proceedings had in such proceeding in quo warranto, shall decree the charter of the corporation forfeited.
@ref 8 Del. C. § 323 (src:1645)
GIVEN failure IS A `s 323 Failure to obey a peremptory writ of mandamus`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 323 the court must decree the charter of the corporation forfeited` failure MEANS
        `s 323 the Attorney General must forthwith commence quo warranto proceedings against the corporation` failure
    AND failure's `the court has competent proof of the failure and proper proceedings have been had in quo warranto`

§§ `s 324 Attachment of shares of stock or any option, right or interest therein; procedure; sale; title upon sale; proceeds`

-- (a) first sentence: what may be attached, for what, and on what condition. Title 6 s 8-102 and s 8-112 are not
-- among the inputs, so whether s 8-112 has been satisfied is an input.
-- src:1649 | The shares of any person in any corporation with all the rights thereto belonging, or any person’s option to acquire the shares, or such person’s right or interest in the shares, may be attached under this section for debt, or other demands, if such person appears on the books of the corporation to hold or own such shares, option, right or interest. …
@ref 8 Del. C. § 324(a) (src:1649)
GIVEN `the attachment is for a debt or other demand` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person appears on the books of the corporation to hold or own the shares, option, right or interest` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 324(a) the shares, option, right or interest may be attached` `the attachment is for a debt or other demand` `the person appears on the books of the corporation to hold or own the shares, option, right or interest` MEANS
        `the attachment is for a debt or other demand`
    AND `the person appears on the books of the corporation to hold or own the shares, option, right or interest`

-- "Except as to an uncertificated security as defined in s 8-102 of Title 6, the attachment is not laid and no order of
-- sale shall issue unless s 8-112 of Title 6 has been satisfied."
-- src:1649 | Except as to an uncertificated security as defined in § 8-102 of Title 6, the attachment is not laid and no order of sale shall issue unless § 8-112 of Title 6 has been satisfied. No order of sale shall be issued until after final judgment shall have been rendered in any case. …
@ref 8 Del. C. § 324(a) (src:1649)
GIVEN `the interest is an uncertificated security as defined in s 8-102 of Title 6` IS A BOOLEAN  -- Title 6 is not among the inputs
      `s 8-112 of Title 6 has been satisfied` IS A BOOLEAN                                     -- Title 6 is not among the inputs
      `final judgment has been rendered in the case` IS A BOOLEAN
      `notice has been given as is required for sales upon execution process` IS A BOOLEAN       -- the law of execution sales is not among the inputs
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 324(a) an order of sale may issue` `the interest is an uncertificated security as defined in s 8-102 of Title 6` `s 8-112 of Title 6 has been satisfied` `final judgment has been rendered in the case` `notice has been given as is required for sales upon execution process` MEANS
        `final judgment has been rendered in the case`
    AND (`the interest is an uncertificated security as defined in s 8-102 of Title 6` OR `s 8-112 of Title 6 has been satisfied`)
    AND `notice has been given as is required for sales upon execution process`

-- src:1649 | Except as to an uncertificated security as defined in § 8-102 of Title 6, the attachment is not laid and no order of sale shall issue unless § 8-112 of Title 6 has been satisfied. …
@ref 8 Del. C. § 324(a) (src:1649)
GIVEN `the interest is an uncertificated security as defined in s 8-102 of Title 6` IS A BOOLEAN
      `s 8-112 of Title 6 has been satisfied` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 324(a) the attachment may be laid` `the interest is an uncertificated security as defined in s 8-102 of Title 6` `s 8-112 of Title 6 has been satisfied` MEANS
    `the interest is an uncertificated security as defined in s 8-102 of Title 6` OR `s 8-112 of Title 6 has been satisfied`

-- "So many of the shares, or so much of the option, right or interest therein may be sold ... as shall be sufficient
-- to satisfy the debt, or other demand, interest and costs": no more may be sold once the proceeds suffice.
-- src:1649 | So many of the shares, or so much of the option, right or interest therein may be sold at public sale to the highest bidder, as shall be sufficient to satisfy the debt, or other demand, interest and costs, …
@ref 8 Del. C. § 324(a) (src:1649)
GIVEN `the amount of the debt or other demand` IS A NUMBER
      `the interest on it` IS A NUMBER
      `the costs` IS A NUMBER
      `the proceeds of the sale so far` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 324(a) the part already sold is sufficient to satisfy the debt, interest and costs` `the amount of the debt or other demand` `the interest on it` `the costs` `the proceeds of the sale so far` MEANS
    `the proceeds of the sale so far` AT LEAST (`the amount of the debt or other demand` PLUS `the interest on it` PLUS `the costs`)

-- Notice of the sale by mail and publication: the order is sent by registered or certified mail, return receipt
-- requested, to the debtor's last known address if the debtor lives out of the county, and published; a debtor who
-- is a nonresident of this State has it mailed and published at least twice for 2 successive weeks, the last
-- publication at least 10 days before the sale, in a newspaper published in the county where the attachment issued.
-- (fork F5: "10 days before the sale" is read as at least 10 days.)
-- src:1649 | If the debtor lives out of the county, a copy of the order shall be sent by registered or certified mail, return receipt requested, to such debtor’s last known address, and shall also be published in a newspaper published in the county of such debtor’s last known residence, if there be any, 10 days before the sale; and if the debtor be a nonresident of this State shall be mailed as aforesaid and published at least twice for 2 successive weeks, the last publication to be at least 10 days before the sale, in a newspaper published in the county where the attachment process issued. …
@ref 8 Del. C. § 324(a) (src:1649)
DECLARE `s 324(a) Notice of the sale` HAS
    `the debtor lives out of the county`                                                                   IS A BOOLEAN
    `the debtor is a nonresident of this State`                                                            IS A BOOLEAN
    `a copy of the order was sent by registered or certified mail, return receipt requested, to the debtor's last known address` IS A BOOLEAN
    `a newspaper is published in the county of the debtor's last known residence`                          IS A BOOLEAN
    `the order was published in a newspaper published in the county of the debtor's last known residence` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the number of times the order was published`                                                          IS A NUMBER
    `the number of successive weeks over which the order was published`                                    IS A NUMBER
    `the order was published in a newspaper published in the county where the attachment process issued`   IS A BOOLEAN
    `the number of days from the last publication to the sale`                                             IS A NUMBER

-- src:1649 | If the debtor lives out of the county, a copy of the order shall be sent by registered or certified mail, return receipt requested, to such debtor’s last known address, and shall also be published in a newspaper published in the county of such debtor’s last known residence, if there be any, 10 days before the sale; and if the debtor be a nonresident of this State shall be mailed as aforesaid and published at least twice for 2 successive weeks, the last publication to be at least 10 days before the sale, in a newspaper published in the county where the attachment process issued. …
@ref 8 Del. C. § 324(a) (src:1649)
GIVEN notice IS A `s 324(a) Notice of the sale`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 324(a) the notice of the sale by mail and publication is sufficient` notice MEANS
    IF notice's `the debtor is a nonresident of this State`
    THEN     notice's `a copy of the order was sent by registered or certified mail, return receipt requested, to the debtor's last known address`
         AND notice's `the order was published in a newspaper published in the county where the attachment process issued`
         AND notice's `the number of times the order was published` AT LEAST 2
         AND notice's `the number of successive weeks over which the order was published` AT LEAST 2
         AND notice's `the number of days from the last publication to the sale` AT LEAST 10
    ELSE IF notice's `the debtor lives out of the county`
         THEN     notice's `a copy of the order was sent by registered or certified mail, return receipt requested, to the debtor's last known address`
              AND (    (NOT notice's `a newspaper is published in the county of the debtor's last known residence`)
                    OR (    notice's `the order was published in a newspaper published in the county of the debtor's last known residence`
                        AND notice's `the number of days from the last publication to the sale` AT LEAST 10))
         ELSE TRUE

-- "If the shares of stock ... be so sold, any assignment, or transfer thereof, by the debtor, after attachment, shall be void."
-- src:1649 | If the shares of stock or any of them or the option to acquire shares or any such right or interest in shares, or any part of them, be so sold, any assignment, or transfer thereof, by the debtor, after attachment, shall be void.
@ref 8 Del. C. § 324(a) (src:1649)
GIVEN `the shares, option, right or interest have been sold` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the debtor assigned or transferred them after the attachment` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 324(a) the debtor's assignment or transfer after attachment is void` `the shares, option, right or interest have been sold` `the debtor assigned or transferred them after the attachment` MEANS
        `the shares, option, right or interest have been sold`
    AND `the debtor assigned or transferred them after the attachment`

-- (b): the certified copy of the process is left with an officer, director or the registered agent in this State
-- (or the corporate registered agent is served as s 321 provides); the corporation must within 20 days after service
-- serve a certificate on the plaintiff.
-- src:1650 | When attachment process issues for shares of stock, or any option to acquire such or any right or interest in such, a certified copy of the process shall be left in this State with any officer or director, or with the registered agent of the corporation. …
-- src:1650 | Service upon a corporate registered agent may be made in the manner provided in § 321 of this title.
@ref 8 Del. C. § 324(b) (src:1650)
GIVEN `a certified copy of the process was left in this State with an officer or director or with the registered agent` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the corporate registered agent was served in the manner provided in s 321` IS A BOOLEAN  -- s 321 is encoded in this module; see `s 321 service of process on the corporation is effective`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 324(b) the process has been served on the corporation` `a certified copy of the process was left in this State with an officer or director or with the registered agent` `the corporate registered agent was served in the manner provided in s 321` MEANS
        `a certified copy of the process was left in this State with an officer or director or with the registered agent`
    OR  `the corporate registered agent was served in the manner provided in s 321`

-- "Within 20 days after service of the process": the twentieth day is inside the period (fork F1).
-- src:1650 | Within 20 days after service of the process, the corporation shall serve upon the plaintiff …
@ref 8 Del. C. § 324(b) (src:1650)
GIVEN `the date the process was served on the corporation` IS A DATE
GIVETH A DATE
`s 324(b) the last day for the corporation to serve the certificate on the plaintiff` `the date the process was served on the corporation` MEANS
    `the date` (`period in days` 20) `after` `the date the process was served on the corporation`

-- src:1650 | Within 20 days after service of the process, the corporation shall serve upon the plaintiff …
@ref 8 Del. C. § 324(b) (src:1650)
GIVEN `the date the process was served on the corporation` IS A DATE
      `the date the corporation served the certificate on the plaintiff` IS A DATE
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 324(b) the corporation served the certificate in time` `the date the process was served on the corporation` `the date the corporation served the certificate on the plaintiff` MEANS
    `the date the corporation served the certificate on the plaintiff` AT MOST (`s 324(b) the last day for the corporation to serve the certificate on the plaintiff` `the date the process was served on the corporation`)

-- What the certificate says: for shares, their number with the number or other marks distinguishing them; for an
-- option, right or interest, it as it appears on the books, in its language and form.
-- src:1650 | the corporation shall serve upon the plaintiff a certificate of the number of shares held or owned by the debtor in the corporation, with the number or other marks distinguishing the same, or in the case the debtor appears on the books of the corporation to have an option to acquire shares of stock or any right or interest in any shares of stock of the corporation, there shall be served upon the plaintiff within 20 days after service of the process a certificate setting forth any such option, right or interest in the shares of the corporation in the language and form in which the option, right or interest appears on the books of the corporation, anything in the certificate of incorporation or bylaws of the corporation to the contrary notwithstanding. …
@ref 8 Del. C. § 324(b) (src:1650)
GIVEN `the debtor appears on the books to hold or own shares` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the certificate gives the number of shares with the number or other marks distinguishing them` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the debtor appears on the books to have an option, right or interest in shares` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the certificate sets forth that option, right or interest in the language and form in which it appears on the books` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 324(b) the certificate states what the subsection requires` `the debtor appears on the books to hold or own shares` `the certificate gives the number of shares with the number or other marks distinguishing them` `the debtor appears on the books to have an option, right or interest in shares` `the certificate sets forth that option, right or interest in the language and form in which it appears on the books` MEANS
        ((NOT `the debtor appears on the books to hold or own shares`) OR `the certificate gives the number of shares with the number or other marks distinguishing them`)
    AND ((NOT `the debtor appears on the books to have an option, right or interest in shares`) OR `the certificate sets forth that option, right or interest in the language and form in which it appears on the books`)

-- "anything in the certificate of incorporation or bylaws of the corporation to the contrary notwithstanding":
-- a provision made anywhere does not relieve the corporation, so no input about such a provision is read.
-- src:1650 | When attachment process issues for shares of stock, or any option to acquire such or any right or interest in such, a certified copy of the process shall be left in this State with any officer or director, or with the registered agent of the corporation. Within 20 days after service of the process, the corporation shall serve upon the plaintiff a certificate of the number of shares held or owned by the debtor in the corporation, with the number or other marks distinguishing the same, or in the case the debtor appears on the books of the corporation to have an option to acquire shares of stock or any right or interest in any shares of stock of the corporation, there shall be served upon the plaintiff within 20 days after service of the process a certificate setting forth any such option, right or interest in the shares of the corporation in the language and form in which the option, right or interest appears on the books of the corporation, anything in the certificate of incorporation or bylaws of the corporation to the contrary notwithstanding. …
@ref 8 Del. C. § 324(b) (src:1650)
GIVEN `where a provision relieving the corporation of the duty is made` IS A `Where a provision is made`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 324(b) a provision of the certificate of incorporation or bylaws relieves the corporation of the duty to serve the certificate` `where a provision relieving the corporation of the duty is made` MEANS
    FALSE

-- (c): the purchaser after a confirmed sale. The stock certificate is left "if any".
-- src:1651 | If, after sale made and confirmed, a certified copy of the order of sale and return and the stock certificate, if any, be left with any officer or director or with the registered agent of the corporation, the purchaser shall be thereby entitled to the shares or any option to acquire shares or any right or interest in shares so purchased, and all income, or dividends which may have been declared, or become payable thereon since the attachment laid. …
@ref 8 Del. C. § 324(c) (src:1651)
GIVEN `the sale has been made and confirmed` IS A BOOLEAN
      `a certified copy of the order of sale and return was left with an officer or director or with the registered agent` IS A BOOLEAN
      `there is a stock certificate` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the stock certificate was left with an officer or director or with the registered agent` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 324(c) the purchaser is entitled to the shares, option, right or interest` `the sale has been made and confirmed` `a certified copy of the order of sale and return was left with an officer or director or with the registered agent` `there is a stock certificate` `the stock certificate was left with an officer or director or with the registered agent` MEANS
        `the sale has been made and confirmed`
    AND `a certified copy of the order of sale and return was left with an officer or director or with the registered agent`
    AND ((NOT `there is a stock certificate`) OR `the stock certificate was left with an officer or director or with the registered agent`)

-- src:1651 | the purchaser shall be thereby entitled to the shares or any option to acquire shares or any right or interest in shares so purchased, and all income, or dividends which may have been declared, or become payable thereon since the attachment laid. …
@ref 8 Del. C. § 324(c) (src:1651)
GIVEN `the purchaser is entitled to the shares, option, right or interest under s 324(c)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the income or dividend was declared or became payable since the attachment was laid` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 324(c) the purchaser is entitled to the income or dividend` `the purchaser is entitled to the shares, option, right or interest under s 324(c)` `the income or dividend was declared or became payable since the attachment was laid` MEANS
        `the purchaser is entitled to the shares, option, right or interest under s 324(c)`
    AND `the income or dividend was declared or became payable since the attachment was laid`

-- "Such sale, returned and confirmed, shall transfer the shares ... as fully as if the debtor ... had transferred the
-- same to such purchaser according to the certificate of incorporation or bylaws of the corporation, anything in the
-- certificate of incorporation or bylaws to the contrary notwithstanding."
-- src:1651 | Such sale, returned and confirmed, shall transfer the shares or the option to acquire shares or any right or interest in shares sold to the purchaser, as fully as if the debtor, or defendant, had transferred the same to such purchaser according to the certificate of incorporation or bylaws of the corporation, anything in the certificate of incorporation or bylaws to the contrary notwithstanding. …
@ref 8 Del. C. § 324(c) (src:1651)
GIVEN `the sale has been returned and confirmed` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 324(c) the sale transfers the shares, option, right or interest to the purchaser despite any contrary provision of the certificate of incorporation or bylaws` `the sale has been returned and confirmed` MEANS
    `the sale has been returned and confirmed`

-- src:1651 | The court which issued the levy and confirmed the sale shall have the power to make an order compelling the corporation, the shares of which were sold, to issue new certificates or uncertificated shares to the purchaser at the sale and to cancel the registration of the shares attached on the books of the corporation upon the giving of an open end bond by such purchaser adequate to protect such corporation.
@ref 8 Del. C. § 324(c) (src:1651)
GIVEN `the court issued the levy and confirmed the sale` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the purchaser has given an open end bond` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the bond is adequate to protect the corporation, as the court finds` IS A BOOLEAN  -- a judgment the text leaves to the court
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 324(c) the court has the power to order the corporation to issue new certificates or uncertificated shares to the purchaser and to cancel the registration` `the court issued the levy and confirmed the sale` `the purchaser has given an open end bond` `the bond is adequate to protect the corporation, as the court finds` MEANS
        `the court issued the levy and confirmed the sale`
    AND `the purchaser has given an open end bond`
    AND `the bond is adequate to protect the corporation, as the court finds`

-- (d): the money arising from the sale is applied "as by law is directed as to the sale of personal property in
-- cases of attachment" (that law is not among the inputs).
-- src:1652 | The money arising from the sale of the shares or from the sale of the option or right or interest shall be applied and paid, by the public official receiving the same, as by law is directed as to the sale of personal property in cases of attachment.
@ref 8 Del. C. § 324(d) (src:1652)
GIVEN `the money arose from the sale of the shares or of the option, right or interest` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 324(d) the money is applied and paid by the public official as the law of attachment of personal property directs` `the money arose from the sale of the shares or of the option, right or interest` MEANS
    `the money arose from the sale of the shares or of the option, right or interest`

§§ `s 325 Actions against officers, directors or stockholders to enforce liability of corporation; unsatisfied judgment against corporation`

-- src:1656 | When the officers, directors or stockholders of any corporation shall be liable by the provisions of this chapter to pay the debts of the corporation, or any part thereof, any person to whom they are liable may have an action, at law or in equity, against any 1 or more of them, …
@ref 8 Del. C. § 325(a) (src:1656)
GIVEN `the defendant is an officer, director or stockholder of the corporation` IS A BOOLEAN
      `a provision of this chapter makes the defendant liable to pay the debts of the corporation or a part of them` IS A BOOLEAN  -- out of range: the provisions that impose such liability (pieces dg1 to dg9, dg11)
      `the plaintiff is a person to whom the defendant is so liable` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 325(a) the plaintiff may sue the defendant at law or in equity` `the defendant is an officer, director or stockholder of the corporation` `a provision of this chapter makes the defendant liable to pay the debts of the corporation or a part of them` `the plaintiff is a person to whom the defendant is so liable` MEANS
        `the defendant is an officer, director or stockholder of the corporation`
    AND `a provision of this chapter makes the defendant liable to pay the debts of the corporation or a part of them`
    AND `the plaintiff is a person to whom the defendant is so liable`

-- src:1656 | and the complaint shall state the claim against the corporation, and the ground on which the plaintiff expects to charge the defendants personally.
@ref 8 Del. C. § 325(a) (src:1656)
GIVEN `the complaint states the claim against the corporation` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the complaint states the ground on which the plaintiff expects to charge the defendants personally` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 325(a) the complaint states what the subsection requires` `the complaint states the claim against the corporation` `the complaint states the ground on which the plaintiff expects to charge the defendants personally` MEANS
        `the complaint states the claim against the corporation`
    AND `the complaint states the ground on which the plaintiff expects to charge the defendants personally`

-- "No suit shall be brought against any officer, director or stockholder for any debt of a corporation of which such
-- person is an officer, director or stockholder, until judgment be obtained therefor against the corporation and
-- execution thereon returned unsatisfied." Both conditions are required (fork F6). A defendant who is none of the
-- three is outside the subsection: not covered.
-- src:1657 | No suit shall be brought against any officer, director or stockholder for any debt of a corporation of which such person is an officer, director or stockholder, until judgment be obtained therefor against the corporation and execution thereon returned unsatisfied.
@ref 8 Del. C. § 325(b) (src:1657)
GIVEN `the defendant is an officer, director or stockholder of the corporation` IS A BOOLEAN
      `judgment has been obtained against the corporation for the debt` IS A BOOLEAN
      `execution on the judgment has been returned unsatisfied` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 325(b) a suit may be brought against the officer, director or stockholder for the debt of the corporation` `the defendant is an officer, director or stockholder of the corporation` `judgment has been obtained against the corporation for the debt` `execution on the judgment has been returned unsatisfied` MEANS
    IF `the defendant is an officer, director or stockholder of the corporation`
    THEN JUST (`judgment has been obtained against the corporation for the debt` AND `execution on the judgment has been returned unsatisfied`)
    ELSE NOTHING

§§ `s 326 Action by officer, director or stockholder against corporation for corporate debt paid`

-- src:1661 | When any officer, director or stockholder shall pay any debt of a corporation for which such person is made liable by the provisions of this chapter, such person may recover the amount so paid in an action against the corporation for money paid for its use, …
@ref 8 Del. C. § 326 (src:1661)
GIVEN `the person is an officer, director or stockholder of the corporation` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person paid a debt of the corporation` IS A BOOLEAN
      `a provision of this chapter makes the person liable for that debt` IS A BOOLEAN  -- out of range: the provisions that impose such liability (pieces dg1 to dg9, dg11)
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 326 the person may recover the amount paid from the corporation` `the person is an officer, director or stockholder of the corporation` `the person paid a debt of the corporation` `a provision of this chapter makes the person liable for that debt` MEANS
        `the person is an officer, director or stockholder of the corporation`
    AND `the person paid a debt of the corporation`
    AND `a provision of this chapter makes the person liable for that debt`

-- The amount that may be recovered is "the amount so paid"; if the section gives no right, nothing under it is
-- recoverable and the question is not answered here (NOTHING).
-- src:1661 | such person may recover the amount so paid in an action against the corporation for money paid for its use, …
@ref 8 Del. C. § 326 (src:1661)
GIVEN `the person may recover from the corporation under s 326` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the amount the person paid` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
`s 326 the amount the person may recover` `the person may recover from the corporation under s 326` `the amount the person paid` MEANS
    IF `the person may recover from the corporation under s 326`
    THEN JUST `the amount the person paid`
    ELSE NOTHING

-- src:1661 | and in such action only the property of the corporation shall be liable to be taken, and not the property of any stockholder.
@ref 8 Del. C. § 326 (src:1661)
GIVEN `the property belongs to the corporation` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 326 the property is liable to be taken in the action` `the property belongs to the corporation` MEANS
    `the property belongs to the corporation`

§§ `s 327 Stockholder's derivative action; allegation of stock ownership`

-- The section requires an averment in the complaint; it does not itself say the plaintiff loses standing without
-- the stock (fork F7).
-- src:1665 | In any derivative suit instituted by a stockholder of a corporation, it shall be averred in the complaint that the plaintiff was a stockholder of the corporation at the time of the transaction of which such stockholder complains or that such stockholder’s stock thereafter devolved upon such stockholder by operation of law.
@ref 8 Del. C. § 327 (src:1665)
GIVEN `the complaint avers that the plaintiff was a stockholder of the corporation at the time of the transaction complained of` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the complaint avers that the plaintiff's stock thereafter devolved upon the plaintiff by operation of law` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 327 the complaint contains the averment of stock ownership that the section requires` `the complaint avers that the plaintiff was a stockholder of the corporation at the time of the transaction complained of` `the complaint avers that the plaintiff's stock thereafter devolved upon the plaintiff by operation of law` MEANS
        `the complaint avers that the plaintiff was a stockholder of the corporation at the time of the transaction complained of`
    OR  `the complaint avers that the plaintiff's stock thereafter devolved upon the plaintiff by operation of law`

§§ `s 328 Effect of liability of corporation on impairment of certain transactions`

-- src:1669 | shall not in any way be lessened or impaired by the sale of its assets, or by the increase or decrease in the capital stock of the corporation, or by its merger or consolidation with 1 or more corporations or by any change or amendment in its certificate of incorporation.
@ref 8 Del. C. § 328 (src:1669)
DECLARE `s 328 Event that does not lessen liability or remedies` IS ONE OF
    `a sale of the assets of the corporation under s 328`
    `an increase in the capital stock of the corporation under s 328`
    `a decrease in the capital stock of the corporation under s 328`
    `a merger or consolidation of the corporation with 1 or more corporations under s 328`
    `a change or amendment in the certificate of incorporation under s 328`
    `an event that s 328 does not list`

-- The liability of the corporation, of its stockholders, directors or officers, and the rights or remedies of its
-- creditors and of persons doing business with it, are not lessened or impaired by any of the five listed events.
-- An event the section does not list is not covered.
-- src:1669 | The liability of a corporation of this State, or the stockholders, directors or officers thereof, or the rights or remedies of the creditors thereof, or of persons doing or transacting business with the corporation, shall not in any way be lessened or impaired by the sale of its assets, or by the increase or decrease in the capital stock of the corporation, or by its merger or consolidation with 1 or more corporations or by any change or amendment in its certificate of incorporation.
@ref 8 Del. C. § 328 (src:1669)
GIVEN `the corporation is a corporation of this State` IS A BOOLEAN
      event IS A `s 328 Event that does not lessen liability or remedies`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 328 the event lessens or impairs the liability or the rights or remedies` `the corporation is a corporation of this State` event MEANS
    IF `the corporation is a corporation of this State`
    THEN (CONSIDER event
          WHEN `an event that s 328 does not list` THEN NOTHING
          OTHERWISE JUST FALSE)
    ELSE NOTHING

§§ `s 329 Defective organization of corporation as defense`

-- src:1673 | No corporation of this State and no person sued by any such corporation shall be permitted to assert the want of legal organization as a defense to any claim.
@ref 8 Del. C. § 329(a) (src:1673)
DECLARE `s 329(a) Party who would assert want of legal organization` IS ONE OF
    `a corporation of this State under s 329(a)`
    `a person sued by a corporation of this State under s 329(a)`
    `another party under s 329(a)`

-- A party the subsection does not name is outside it: not covered (NOTHING).
-- src:1673 | No corporation of this State and no person sued by any such corporation shall be permitted to assert the want of legal organization as a defense to any claim.
@ref 8 Del. C. § 329(a) (src:1673)
GIVEN party IS A `s 329(a) Party who would assert want of legal organization`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 329(a) the party is permitted to assert want of legal organization as a defense to a claim` party MEANS
    CONSIDER party
    WHEN `a corporation of this State under s 329(a)` THEN JUST FALSE
    WHEN `a person sued by a corporation of this State under s 329(a)` THEN JUST FALSE
    OTHERWISE NOTHING

-- src:1674 | This section shall not be construed to prevent judicial inquiry into the regularity or validity of the organization of a corporation, or its lawful possession of any corporate power it may assert in any other suit or proceeding where its corporate existence or the power to exercise the corporate rights it asserts is challenged, and evidence tending to sustain the challenge shall be admissible in any such suit or proceeding.
@ref 8 Del. C. § 329(b) (src:1674)
GIVEN `the corporation asserts its corporate existence or a corporate power in a suit or proceeding` IS A BOOLEAN
      `that corporate existence or the power to exercise the corporate rights is challenged` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 329(b) judicial inquiry into the regularity or validity of the organization or the lawful possession of the power is not prevented` `the corporation asserts its corporate existence or a corporate power in a suit or proceeding` `that corporate existence or the power to exercise the corporate rights is challenged` MEANS
        `the corporation asserts its corporate existence or a corporate power in a suit or proceeding`
    AND `that corporate existence or the power to exercise the corporate rights is challenged`

-- src:1674 | and evidence tending to sustain the challenge shall be admissible in any such suit or proceeding.
@ref 8 Del. C. § 329(b) (src:1674)
GIVEN `the corporation asserts its corporate existence or a corporate power in a suit or proceeding` IS A BOOLEAN
      `that corporate existence or the power to exercise the corporate rights is challenged` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 329(b) evidence tending to sustain the challenge is admissible` `the corporation asserts its corporate existence or a corporate power in a suit or proceeding` `that corporate existence or the power to exercise the corporate rights is challenged` MEANS
        `the corporation asserts its corporate existence or a corporate power in a suit or proceeding`
    AND `that corporate existence or the power to exercise the corporate rights is challenged`

§§ `s 330 Usury; pleading by corporation`

-- src:1678 | No corporation shall plead any statute against usury in any court of law or equity in any suit instituted to enforce the payment of any bond, note or other evidence of indebtedness issued or assumed by it.
@ref 8 Del. C. § 330 (src:1678)
GIVEN `the suit is to enforce payment of a bond, note or other evidence of indebtedness issued or assumed by the corporation` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 330 the corporation may plead a statute against usury` `the suit is to enforce payment of a bond, note or other evidence of indebtedness issued or assumed by the corporation` MEANS
    IF `the suit is to enforce payment of a bond, note or other evidence of indebtedness issued or assumed by the corporation`
    THEN JUST FALSE
    ELSE NOTHING
